.TH EUCLID-CLI-ENS-LIST-SUBSCRIPTIONS 1 "August 2026" "euclid-cli 1.0.33" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-ens-list-subscriptions \- list the subscriptions of a topic
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli ens list-subscriptions
.BR \-\-topic | \-t
.I TOPIC-ERN
.SH DESCRIPTION
Lists every subscription fanning out from a topic, identified by its
Euclid resource name (ERN). Each subscription is printed with its own
ERN (usable with
.BR euclid-cli-ens-unsubscribe (1)),
its type, and its target ERN.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-topic " " \fITOPIC-ERN\fR
Euclid resource name of the topic whose subscriptions are listed.
Required.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The topic's subscriptions are printed as JSON (an empty list if it has
none).
.TP
.B 1
Missing/invalid arguments, or the server could not be reached.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 ens list-subscriptions \e
    --topic ern:ens:eu-central-1:000000000000:topic:order-events
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR euclid-cli-ens (1),
.BR euclid-cli-ens-subscribe (1),
.BR euclid-cli-ens-unsubscribe (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Jens Vogt <jens.vogt@opitz-consulting.com>
